{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. e3 Nf6 5. b3 Bd6 6. Bb2 O-O 7. Nd2 Re8 8. Ne2 Be6 9. a3 Qd7 10. h3 Rad8 { Plan: Resolve king safety and choose c4, d4 or e4 as a central challenge. Identify which bishop will become active after the chosen break. Opponent resource: Black has more space and can prepare ...e4 or ...d4. White's extra tempo has not prevented a central bind. } *

[Event "HW-02 Black develops Be7"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
[Round "-"]
[White "White study side"]
[Black "Black study side"]
[Result "*"]

{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 Be7 5. b3 O-O 6. Bb2 Nc6 7. Nd2 { Authored anchor. Black develops modestly and keeps the center intact. White preserves flexibility while the bishops watch long diagonals. } 7... Re8 8. h3 Bd6 9. Ngf3 h6 10. O-O Bf5 { Plan: Choose Ne2 or Ngf3 according to the desired break, then castle when safe. c4 can question d5 without first building a large center. Opponent resource: Black may use ...Re8 and ...Bf8 to prepare central expansion. Quiet development can support a serious squeeze. } *

