[White "White study side"]
[Black "Black study side"]
[Result "*"]

{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. d3 g6 4. e3 Bg7 5. b3 O-O 6. Bb2 c5 7. Nd2 { Authored anchor. Black combines central space with a fianchetto. White's b2 bishop points toward the opposing king side, but central pawns may block its influence. } 7... Qc7 8. Ngf3 Nc6 9. O-O e5 10. c4 d4 { Plan: Complete development and decide whether c4 or e4 best opens your bishops. Count the pressure on b2 after the center clears. Opponent resource: Black can advance ...d4 and restrict the b1 knight. The g7 bishop may become stronger than its white counterpart after exchanges. } *

