{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e6 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 Be7 5. b3 O-O 6. Bb2 c5 7. Nd2 { Authored anchor. Black has a stable d5-e6 center but has not occupied e5. White has time to prepare a direct central challenge. } 7... Nc6 8. Ngf3 b5 9. O-O Qc7 10. c4 bxc4 { Plan: Consider Ngf3 and e4, or Ne2 and c4. Choose one coherent route rather than moving both knights repeatedly without a central goal. Opponent resource: ...Nc6 and ...e5 can gain more space. Do not wait for Black to complete every central ambition before responding. } *

