{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 e5 2. Bg2 d6 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 g6 5. b3 Bg7 6. Bb2 O-O 7. Nd2 { Authored anchor. Black's d6 pawn supports e5 and keeps the center flexible. White can choose a partial Hippo or a more active King's Indian Attack structure. } 7... a5 8. a4 Nc6 9. e4 Ne8 10. Ne2 f5 { Plan: Compare e4 with c4 and develop the king knight to support that choice. Decide whether the b2 bishop has useful pressure before exchanging e-pawns. Opponent resource: Black can use ...Nc6 and ...Be6 to develop with central influence. A later ...d5 may seize the initiative if White waits too long. } *

