{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 g6 2. Bg2 Bg7 3. d3 d6 4. Nf3 Nf6 5. e3 e6 6. b3 b6 7. Bb2 Bb7 8. Nbd2 Nbd7 { Authored anchor. Both sides restrain the center, but the knights on f3 and f6 block the opposing fianchetto diagonals before b-pawn moves expose the corner rooks. This detail prevents a tactical accident. } 9. b4 c5 10. a3 O-O { Plan: Use the first move to develop and choose a central claim such as e4 or c4. Castling may be more valuable than automatically adding a3 and h3. Opponent resource: Without a blocker on the long diagonal, b3 or ...b6 can expose a corner rook to the enemy bishop. Never build this formation without tracing the diagonal. } *

