{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 c5 4. e3 Nc6 5. b3 Nf6 6. Bb2 Be7 { Authored anchor. Black establishes c5-d5-e5. White must challenge the center before completing every wing pawn move. } 7. Ne2 h5 8. h3 Qc7 9. O-O Bf5 10. f4 e4 { Plan: Develop a knight to support c4 or e4, and calculate the resulting exchanges. Consider whether a partial formation gives more active play than the complete shell. Opponent resource: ...d4 can close the center with a large space advantage. If every white piece lacks squares, the setup has become too slow. } *

