{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 e5 2. Bg2 d5 3. d3 f5 4. e3 Nf6 5. Ne2 { Authored anchor. White develops the king knight and prepares king safety against Black's ambitious center. Delaying b3 can be sensible when the center needs urgent attention. } 5... Be6 6. O-O h5 7. c4 dxc4 8. Bxb7 Nbd7 9. h4 Rb8 10. Bg2 cxd3 { Plan: Compare c4 and f4 only after calculating captures and king exposure. A supported e4 break may also change the central balance. Opponent resource: Black may push ...e4 or ...f4 with tempo. A slow double fianchetto can become a target if the center opens before White castles. } *

