{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. e3 d4 5. exd4 exd4 { Authored anchor. White exchanges the invading pawn and changes the structure. Black retains a d4 wedge, but White has opened a diagonal and can attack the pawn. } 6. Nf3 Nf6 7. O-O Be7 8. a3 a5 9. c3 O-O 10. Qa4 dxc3 { Plan: Develop Ne2 or Nf3 and target d4 with c3 when safe. Decide whether the queen bishop belongs on b2 or a more direct square. Opponent resource: The d4 pawn restricts Nc3 and may support a central outpost. Do not place a knight where an enemy pawn can simply capture it. } *

[Event "HW-10 Black advances ...e4 early"]
[Site "Original study material"]
[Date "????.??.??"]
