[White "White study side"]
[Black "Black study side"]
[Result "*"]

{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 e4 5. dxe4 Nxe4 { Authored anchor. The central exchange releases Black's knight onto e4. White has prevented a permanent pawn wedge but must now address the active piece. } 6. Nd2 Nxd2 7. Bxd2 c6 8. Bc3 Nd7 9. e4 dxe4 10. Nh3 Nc5 { Plan: Develop with pressure on e4 and keep the queen and king safe along opened files. Choose a knight square that helps challenge the outpost. Opponent resource: A central knight can threaten forks on c3 or f2 depending on the position. Check its concrete attacks before making another pawn move. } *

