{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 d4 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. O-O { Authored anchor. White abandons the strict Ne2 formation and develops quickly against Black's space. Nf3 is a practical adaptation when central pressure matters more than symmetry. } 5... Bc5 6. Nbd2 Nge7 7. Ne4 Bb6 8. b4 a6 9. c3 dxc3 10. Nxc3 O-O { Plan: Use e3 or c3 to undermine d4, and bring out the queen knight to support the chosen break. Opponent resource: Black can consolidate with ...Nf6 and ...Be7. Further waiting can let the d4 pawn become a permanent restriction. } *

