{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 c6 3. d3 e5 4. e3 Nf6 5. b3 Bd6 6. Bb2 { Authored anchor. Black supports d5 and may expand with ...e4. White's b2 bishop puts indirect pressure on e5, but that pressure depends on the central pawn contacts. } 6... O-O 7. Nd2 Re8 8. Ngf3 h6 9. O-O Bf5 10. e4 Bh7 { Plan: Develop a knight and calculate c4 as a challenge to d5. Complete king safety before opening the center widely. Opponent resource: ...e4 can gain space and attack useful squares. Do not count a bishop as attacking through your own e3 pawn. } *

