{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 h5 2. Nf3 h4 3. Nxh4 { Authored anchor. Black attacks the g3 pawn before building a center. Nf3 develops and can capture on h4 when Black advances without support. } 3... e5 4. e4 Nc6 5. d3 d5 6. exd5 Qxd5 7. Bg2 Qe6 8. a3 Bd7 9. O-O O-O-O 10. Re1 Nge7 { Plan: Return the knight to a useful square if attacked and complete development. Accepting a pawn is useful only if it does not cost excessive time or king safety. Opponent resource: Black may strike in the center while the knight sits on the rim. Do not keep chasing pawns instead of developing. } *

