{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. e3 h5 5. h3 { Authored anchor. White restrains ...h4 by preparing to meet the pawn contact on favorable terms. This is a specific defensive decision, not a requirement to play h3 in every Hippo. } 5... Be6 6. a3 a5 7. Nc3 Qd7 8. b3 Be7 9. Nf3 f6 10. Qe2 g5 { Plan: Develop quickly and consider central counterplay. If ...h4 arrives, calculate gxh4 and exchanges rather than assuming the wing is locked. Opponent resource: Black can prepare ...g5 or castle long. A pawn on h3 can become a hook if the rest of the position is neglected. } *

