{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. e3 g5 { Authored anchor. Black gains kingside space while delaying development. White should look for central action and king safety rather than merely copying a pawn wall. } 5. Nc3 Be6 6. e4 d4 7. Nd5 h5 8. h4 g4 9. c3 Nce7 10. Bg5 Bg7 { Plan: Examine c4 or h4 concretely and develop knights. Choose the king's destination after assessing whether the g- and h-files may open. Opponent resource: Black can play ...h5-h4 and gain attacking tempi. A passive reply may turn a premature advance into a strong attack. } *

