{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. Nf3 Be6 5. O-O Qd7 6. b3 Bh3 7. Bxh3 Qxh3 { Authored anchor. Black exchanges the g2 bishop and brings the queen toward White's already castled king. White's knight has left g1, so the queen on h3 cannot simply be captured by that knight. } 8. e4 Nf6 9. exd5 Nxd5 10. Re1 f6 { Plan: Inspect checks and dark-square threats, develop with tempo if available and look for central counterplay. The king is already on g1, so the task is defending the actual shelter. Opponent resource: If White's knight were still on g1, ...Qxh3 would lose the queen to Nxh3. In this line its different square makes the attack a real concern. } *

