{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nc6 4. e3 Nf6 5. b3 a5 6. Bb2 a4 { Authored anchor. Black attacks the b3 structure and seeks open queenside lines. White must calculate the pawn contact before adding a routine knight move. } 7. a3 axb3 8. cxb3 Bg4 9. Nf3 Bd6 10. h3 Bf5 { Plan: Compare bxa4 with a3 and central counterplay, including rook files and bishop activity after the exchanges. Opponent resource: The b2 bishop and a1 rook can become targets when files open. A queenside attack may matter even if your king plans to castle short. } *

