{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 e5 2. Bg2 d5 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 Bb4+ 5. Bd2 { Authored anchor. The bishop check interrupts the setup. Bd2 develops while blocking; the queen bishop does not have to reach b2 in every game. } 5... a5 6. a3 Bc5 7. Nf3 Nc6 8. Bc3 d4 9. exd4 exd4 10. Bd2 h6 { Plan: Complete development and decide whether a later bishop exchange improves coordination. Keep the central pawns supported and castle when safe. Opponent resource: Moving a pawn to block without checking the resulting weaknesses may cost time. A fixed formation is no reason to choose an inferior response to check. } *

