{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 e5 3. d3 Nf6 4. Nf3 Nc6 5. O-O Be7 6. c4 { Authored anchor. White challenges d5 with active development and a castled king. This useful departure resembles a Reti or reversed King's Indian structure more than a complete Hippo. } 6... O-O 7. cxd5 Nxd5 8. Nc3 Be6 9. Bd2 Qd7 10. a3 a5 { Plan: Compare ...d4, ...dxc4 and maintaining tension. Develop the queen side according to the resulting pawn structure. Opponent resource: If Black closes with ...d4, Nc3 may be restricted. Plan the knight route before fixing every pawn. } *

