{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 d5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. d3 e6 4. Nf3 Be7 5. O-O O-O 6. Nbd2 c5 7. e4 { Authored anchor. White adopts a King's Indian Attack center because Black's structure makes it useful. The b-pawn remains flexible instead of being committed automatically. } 7... Nc6 8. Re1 Qc7 9. c3 h6 10. Qe2 Rd8 { Plan: Support e4, then assess e5 and the available knight routes. Use the KIA course for deeper study of this exact center. Opponent resource: Black can exchange on e4 or advance ...d4. Do not assume the e5 attack is available in every branch. } *

