{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 g6 2. Bg2 Bg7 3. d3 d6 4. e3 Nf6 5. Ne2 O-O 6. O-O e5 7. d4 { Authored anchor. White uses development and king safety to justify a central claim. The d-pawn advances only after the pieces are ready to cope with exchanges. } 7... e4 8. b4 Re8 9. c4 h5 10. Nbc3 Bf5 { Plan: Calculate ...exd4 and ...Nc6, then develop the queen side to useful squares. Compare the activity of the g2 bishop after the center opens. Opponent resource: Advancing d4 may leave e3 weak or open lines for Black too. A central gain is not free of structural consequences. } *

