{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 e5 2. Bg2 d5 3. d3 Nf6 4. e3 e4 5. dxe4 dxe4 6. Qxd8+ Kxd8 { Authored anchor. The exchanges open the d-file and allow White to remove queens. Black loses castling rights, but with queens gone the main issue is piece activity and pawn targets. } 7. Ne2 Bf5 8. Nd2 Bc5 9. b3 Nbd7 10. Bb2 c6 { Plan: Develop the knights, assess the e4 pawn and activate the king when safe. Do not keep playing for a direct king attack without queens. Opponent resource: Black's centralized king may become useful if the position simplifies further. A lost castling right alone does not prove an advantage. } *

