{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 f5 2. Bg2 Nf6 3. d3 g6 4. Nf3 Bg7 5. O-O O-O 6. c4 { Authored anchor. White develops actively and challenges the center with c4 rather than waiting for a full double fianchetto. Black's f-pawn commitment helps define the dark-square battle. } 6... d6 7. Nc3 Nc6 8. Rb1 a5 9. a3 e5 10. b4 axb4 { Plan: Prepare Nc3 and e4 if justified, or contest d5 directly. Keep an eye on the g7 bishop and Black's potential ...e5 break. Opponent resource: Black can build a strong kingside attack if given too much time. Do not answer every threat with a small pawn move. } *

