{ Original Hippopotamus as White course. Study material, not a historical game. } 1. g3 b6 2. Bg2 Nc6 3. e4 Bb7 4. d3 e6 5. Nd2 Nf6 6. Ngf3 { Authored anchor. Black blocks the g2-b7 diagonal with Nc6 before putting the bishop on b7. White uses the flank development to establish a central foothold. } 6... d5 7. e5 Nd7 8. d4 Ba6 9. a3 Ne7 10. b4 c5 { Plan: Castle, support e4 and compare central exchanges. The position may become a KIA-style game rather than a complete Hippo. Opponent resource: Immediate ...Bb7 without a blocker would leave that bishop available to Bxb7. Check the long diagonal before assuming a normal fianchetto is safe. } *

